IS  - 0310-057X (Linking)
VI  - 30
IP  - 3
DP  - 2002 Jun
TI  - Total intravenous anaesthesia for tracheobronchial stenting in children.
PG  - 376-9
AB  - Stenosis and malacia of the tracheobronchial tree, most often secondary to 
      prolonged intubation, tracheostomy or following correction of a congenital 
      cardiac lesion, present a significant therapeutic problem, especially when the 
      lesions are extensive. The utilization of self-expanding tracheobronchial stents 
      is a useful addition to the medical armamentarium for maintenance of airways in 
      these patients with major airway stenosis and collapse. The majority of previous 
      reported cases of tracheobronchial stenting have been performed under general 
      anaesthesia with the help of rigid bronchoscopy under direct vision. We conducted 
      two cases of tracheobronchial stenting in postoperative cardiosurgical babies 
      under continuous propofol infusion taking advantage of cardiovascular stability 
      during continuous infusion and rapid emergence after its discontinuation.
