DP  - 2006 Jun
TI  - Long-term management of polychondritis with serial tracheobronchial stents.
PG  - e24-6
AB  - A 56-year-old woman was referred to our hospital for airway compromise. Relapsing 
      polychondritis was diagnosed by bronchial cartilage biopsy. Bronchoscopy showed 
      tracheobronchial malacia due to the disappearance of bronchial cartilage as a 
      result of chondritis. Stent insertion using a Dynamic stent (Rüsch; Kernen, 
      Germany), Ultraflex stent (Boston Scientific International, Colombes, France) and 
      TM stent (Fuji Systems Corp, Tokyo, Japan) was repeated for more than 7 years. 
      Dramatic improvement of dyspnea was obtained each time. The patient survived 
      during this period without oxygen inhalation or mechanical ventilation before she 
      suddenly died due to suffocation caused by difficulty of sputum discharge.
